# ooda — workflow driver
File: website/pulled/ooda.oot

Source: openOODA/ooda/docs/

## What it is

The `ooda` binary. Tag v0.2.7. It compiles, runs, tests, and
formats `.oo` files. It spawns `opm`, `lsp`, and `mcp` as
separate packages. It does not contain the compiler.

## Install

```
curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install.sh | bash
```

## Surface

13 in-process commands (from `ooda/docs/COMMANDS.oot`):

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `ooda build` | Compile with oodac |
| `ooda run` | Compile and execute |
| `ooda gen` | Scaffold a `.oo` file |
| `ooda test` | Run one test file |
| `ooda install` | Install a release pack |
| `ooda bench` | Time `oodac check` |
| `ooda init` | New project layout |
| `ooda context` | List `.oo` files or stream the codex |
| `ooda health` | Print `ooda health: ok` |
| `ooda fix` | Apply at most 8 diagnostic edits |
| `ooda digest` | SHA-256 of a file |
| `ooda fmt` | Format `.oo` in place |
| `ooda token` | Token ledger subcommands |

Spawned: `ooda opm`, `ooda lsp`, `ooda mcp`. Those binaries
live under `$OODACODEX/bin/`. OODACODEX is required.

`ooda token` subcommands: status, report, audit, query, ask,
schema, diff, tail, fix, snapshot, enforce, extra.
